{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place","id":995472,"title":"How many mages do you see in a single place?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-29T18:57:30-07:00","id":995472,"title":"How many mages do you see in a single place?","content":"I've been constructing a game world for my home city(Miami), which has gone swimmingly except for how many Mages should be here. I've described about 400 members of the Pentacle existing in the Consilium, which branches out into Monroe County(Key Largo, Key West, Islamorada, etc), all of Dade, and all of Broward County as well as all the way up to Port St. Lucie to an extent. How many Mages do you put into your Chronicles, if not as important NPC's but also as background characters that exist in passing? Note: of the 400, most of them are not Mages, but rather Sleepwalkers and lesser supernaturals that aid the Mages in drudge work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T19:39:27-07:00","id":995480,"title":"","content":"That's a lot. In my Miami setting there's about three, since most of them were killed. But they were never into the triple digits to begin with.<br /> <br /> Do you really need a hard number, or can you just go with what the story requires?<br /> <br /> Going by other settings people use, the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970181#post970181\"> New York City</a> one is the largest consilium in the western world in, I think, Travis Stout's games.<br /> <br /> Sorry, right, I forgot to answer question. I'm building another mage setting right now, in Michigan of all places. I think the setup I have would traditionally be two consilia but they're spread out and alone each don't really have the organization to manage to be a consilium on their own. I haven't really set a number to it, and I'm not done building. I'm guessing conservatively it will come to almost 20 relevant NPCs, at least upon creation, and probably 20 'irrelevant' ones that have names and identities but aren't expected to be a big part of things, then a gaggle who will be there but probably won't show up like 42's cabalmates. That's not counting things like a solitary at the edge of town or cabal who likely won't have an appearance in the story. And I fully expect the numbers to shift around a bit as its often up to the players, finally, to decide who's relevant or not.<br /> <br /> That isn't counting familiars, proximi, guardians and so forth. Though I do have some of those ready. It is counting left-handed and traitors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-30-2016, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:21:52-07:00","id":995500,"title":"","content":"I'm basically going with what the story requires, I've got one cabal of FC, and there's the Arrow Caucus but that's not really a cabal. Other than that, I have a possibly SL mixed cabal planned, but no hard and fast anything on that front, and then one loner Seer (Maybe), one loner Nameless, and whatever Sleepwalkers I feel like sprinkling in (Can blame one of my players for at least one cult that will be springing up in the area). I figure the number of participants will evolve naturally to what I need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T22:21:23-07:00","id":995514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=995500#post995500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm basically going with what the story requires, I've got one cabal of FC, and there's the Arrow Caucus but that's not really a cabal. Other than that, I have a possibly SL mixed cabal planned, but no hard and fast anything on that front, and then one loner Seer (Maybe), one loner Nameless, and whatever Sleepwalkers I feel like sprinkling in (Can blame one of my players for at least one cult that will be springing up in the area). I figure the number of participants will evolve naturally to what I need.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This probably seems the best idea. So far I have several cabals planned for local flavor, from the Storm Keepers living in an abandoned lighthouse on a fictional island off of Key Biscayne I made just for them, to the group of Thyrsus who deal with bizarre spirits in the Everglades, along with the Uratha who hunt there, and several Nameless groups that are full of a Proximus Dynasty discovered in the Carribean by Spanish Thearchs when they arrived several centuries prior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T02:53:12-07:00","id":995564,"title":"","content":"We have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city\">general topic on population ratios of supernatura</a>l in <b>CoD</b> games...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:52:54-07:00","id":995812,"title":"","content":"My suggestions, aside reading the topic linked above:<br /> <br /> First, don't think too much about that in such definite numbers. You don't have to determine everything right now, leave space for the future.<br /> <br /> Second, keep it low at first. It is your call if the city is full of Mages or have just a handful of them, but you don't need to decide that yet. Stay firstly conservative, do just what you need, and see during play what you need more. If you do too much at first it can get out of hand without much room for &quot;correction&quot;, and you'll probably never have opportunity to use most of the material.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb: you need an NPC to &quot;command&quot; each group you want to be a part of the city's social structure. It isn't about every possible group of the game, but only the ones that make your city tick. Could be a member of each order of the Pentacle on most cities, though you can introduce a Nameless Order and/or eliminate a member of the Pentacle as a part of your structure. You'll need also 2 or 3 &quot;quest-givers&quot;, NPCs that look for the players to deliver plot hooks. Only 1 other member for each group, and maybe 1 of neither, will be enough for the players to deal on a daily basis and have the &quot;society impression&quot;.<br /> <br /> That gives you 12 to 14 NPCs to give the players the full impression of a structured society with 5 different groups. There are ways to do with less than that at start, but with your style I'll say that it is enough. The players will take some time to ever deal with more than this at a social level, doesn't matter how big the city. From that, only do what you need for specific reasons, and see how things develop. Even if you need a bigger society, firstly you won't need to flesh-out more than those characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:00:55-07:00","id":995818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=995812#post995812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule of thumb: you need an NPC to &quot;command&quot; each group you want to be a part of the city's social structure. It isn't about every possible group of the game, but only the ones that make your city tick. Could be a member of each order of the Pentacle on most cities,</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point, though depending on your 'tier' of the game you might have them know who the leader is but only actually deal with a 'face' character. This is backed up in the text with the Guardians, for instance, keeping their Epopt secret and communicating primarily through Emissaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:40:50-07:00","id":995880,"title":"","content":"Indeed. The only characters that need to be really fleshed-out for now are the ones the PCs are likely to deal soon. Leaders tend to be more mysterious and out-of-reach, unless the city is really short in mages.<br /> <br /> There will be variations, of course, but if the city is big enough to actually have any sort of hierarchy, then the upper echelons aren't easily available. Some will try to be close to their &quot;subjects&quot;, of course, but even then the PCs won't have so much attention or opportunity at first. Those people don't need to be fleshed-out except for what the players are actually going to see or interact with. The same can be said of others, but the players are more likely to snoop into their affairs or simply have more access if they have the interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:50:53-07:00","id":995883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=995480#post995480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot. In my Miami setting there's about three, since most of them were killed. But they were never into the triple digits to begin with.<br /> <br /> Do you really need a hard number, or can you just go with what the story requires?<br /> <br /> Going by other settings people use, the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970181#post970181\"> New York City</a> one is the largest consilium in the western world in, I think, Travis Stout's games.<br /> <br /> Sorry, right, I forgot to answer question. I'm building another mage setting right now, in Michigan of all places. I think the setup I have would traditionally be two consilia but they're spread out and alone each don't really have the organization to manage to be a consilium on their own. I haven't really set a number to it, and I'm not done building. I'm guessing conservatively it will come to almost 20 relevant NPCs, at least upon creation, and probably 20 'irrelevant' ones that have names and identities but aren't expected to be a big part of things, then a gaggle who will be there but probably won't show up like 42's cabalmates. That's not counting things like a solitary at the edge of town or cabal who likely won't have an appearance in the story. And I fully expect the numbers to shift around a bit as its often up to the players, finally, to decide who's relevant or not.<br /> <br /> That isn't counting familiars, proximi, guardians and so forth. Though I do have some of those ready. It is counting left-handed and traitors.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always figured the LA one was rather large - huge area to draw on, large number of people, the presence of Hollywood and the weirdness of Goetia there.<br /> <br /> There's also the weird split between the Consilium and the Assembly. I have trouble imagining there <i>aren't</i> triple digits of mages living there, even if not all of them talk to one another. Twenty or so cabals could find space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:05:52-07:00","id":995889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=995883#post995883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always figured the LA one was rather large - huge area to draw on, large number of people, the presence of Hollywood and the weirdness of Goetia there.<br /> <br /> There's also the weird split between the Consilium and the Assembly. I have trouble imagining there <i>aren't</i> triple digits of mages living there, even if not all of them talk to one another. Twenty or so cabals could find space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing keeps you from putting that many mages there in your games.<br /> <br /> They haven't put numbers in most of the settings. This is a good thing. You can put however many you want. And you're right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-30-2016, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:37:51-07:00","id":995916,"title":"","content":"In special, Mage is among the games with more freedom for numbers. They don't feed on humans or otherwise threaten human life with their own existence, they don't have a hard time hiding (though they do hiding their works), their concepts and powers don't inherently require population control or secrecy through little numbers. Nor their way of coming to be is linked in any known way to population statistics.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, the city can have as many Mages as you want. I'll say that it could have as much as 1% its population as Awakened without threatening the setting-as-written. As I said in the thread about supernatural population, it would certainly have consequences for such great numbers, but nothing too problematic.<br /> <br /> What I question is the need for numbers. And not in the sense of saying you shouldn't have many Mages. But precisely in the sense of evaluating how many you will actually need, because it is:<br /> A) Too easy to overestimate the number needed;<br /> B) Too hard to correct it if it becomes too great to have the desired effect (unless when mass killing is enough, of course).<br /> <br /> For further advice: remember that you can always look outside the current city on time and space for help. You don't need every Mage to already be in the city, because there are Mages who live in the wilderness or the outskirts, there are Mages who travel, and there are Mages who are yet to Awaken. On the same token, there are Mages who are going to leave the city or to die at some point in the chronicle. And you don't need to keep track of everything, instead of justifying whatever you need to do with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T20:01:44-07:00","id":995928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=995916#post995916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I question is the need for numbers. And not in the sense of saying you shouldn't have many Mages. But precisely in the sense of evaluating how many you will actually need, because it is:<br /> A) Too easy to overestimate the number needed;<br /> B) Too hard to correct it if it becomes too great to have the desired effect (unless when mass killing is enough, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been what got me about wanting hard numbers. It makes sense if one of your players is a mage census taker, but providing you have a decent sized high school, college, workplace or neighborhood, the exact number of people within would be a guess, unless you had the numbers from another source. And from a storytelling standpoint there's no problem with a long-running game to introduce a 'new' cabal. 'At the consilium you see the Pandoran Vox cabal, they don't normally show up and their leader looks anxious about something.' Or alternatively not mention them at all because they're not standing out. 'Representatives of all the city's cabals and a few from outside the consilium are here.' Which can be done without naming all of them, and the cabals they represent, and each member of their cabal, and their proximi and familiar.<br /> <br /> Plus obviously if you create everything, then get a new book or homebrew something or just follow the plot and want to introduce something from it, you've potentially built yourself in a corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T21:33:41-07:00","id":995952,"title":"","content":"My experience in actually running things is that numbers help you understand the kind of atmosphere you're trying to create and keep consistent.A city with ten Pentacle Mages will feel <i>very</i> different than one with a hundred. A small town with twenty Awakened souls will feel very different than one with three or four. Knowing how many sorcerers there are gives you a sensation of how &quot;crowded&quot; the magical landscape is and that, in turn, adds to sensations of intimacy and distance; of claustrophobia and isolation.<br /> <br /> I don't need a precise headcount to know how many people there are, but having a consistent idea of how many there are gives you boundaries to build in. It's much easier to build something with some measure of definition than it is to just wing it and then later realize you've ended up creating a vastly inconsistent sensation in your setting.<br /> <br /> I like to know the rough &quot;Mage density&quot; for a region I'm running games in because it helps me figure how to make things feel.<br /> <br /> If you need to tweak something, that's not a big deal because your player's characters never have exact numbers. Ultimately, it's just for creating a sense of atmosphere and understanding how consequences will play out. Again, different numbers give different feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T02:51:50-07:00","id":996009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=995928#post995928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has always been what got me about wanting hard numbers. It makes sense if one of your players is a mage census taker, but providing you have a decent sized high school, college, workplace or neighborhood, the exact number of people within would be a guess, unless you had the numbers from another source.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've wondered about that but the difficulty is that Consilia almost certainly do have reigsters of members. I mean, you generally need to actively join a consilium which almost certainly means swearing some kind of oath which probably needs to be recorded somewhere. At minimum I'd expect the consilium to have a list of affiliated cabals.<br /> <br /> Now, that register is probably not open to the Awakened public, but the fact that a list exists makes it seem a little implausible that the rough number of members/cabals wouldn't be fairly common knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T03:59:12-07:00","id":996018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=995952#post995952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience in actually running things is that numbers help you understand the kind of atmosphere you're trying to create and keep consistent.A city with ten Pentacle Mages will feel <i>very</i> different than one with a hundred. A small town with twenty Awakened souls will feel very different than one with three or four. Knowing how many sorcerers there are gives you a sensation of how &quot;crowded&quot; the magical landscape is and that, in turn, adds to sensations of intimacy and distance; of claustrophobia and isolation.<br /> <br /> I don't need a precise headcount to know how many people there are, but having a consistent idea of how many there are gives you boundaries to build in. It's much easier to build something with some measure of definition than it is to just wing it and then later realize you've ended up creating a vastly inconsistent sensation in your setting.<br /> <br /> I like to know the rough &quot;Mage density&quot; for a region I'm running games in because it helps me figure how to make things feel.<br /> <br /> If you need to tweak something, that's not a big deal because your player's characters never have exact numbers. Ultimately, it's just for creating a sense of atmosphere and understanding how consequences will play out. Again, different numbers give different feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree, but that's the point. Define the rough numbers based on need, not in estimates and hard numbers. My suggestion is about what you need to have defined at hand to built some sense of society without having to define further before you get a hand of it. It isn't about guessing how many mages will be there, but about not putting yourself in a corner.<br /> <br /> @<b>Michael</b>, I'll borrow a little the exemple of the school. A high school is also bound to have a precise register of every student, and their years and classes. But how many of them actually know even an approximation of those numbers? It isn't that the information isn't present or available, but that it won't play a role on most people's lives. You can actually have a non-registered student in the middle without no one ever noticing, it is a fairly common trope.<br /> <br /> Rough numbers is something good to have at hand, when you already know what you want out of the game. It helps to create a given feel in the game, and let the ST show the control the local Concilia have over their registers. But those numbers shouldn't be defined <u>before</u> you know what you're wanting, the local Concilia not <u>always</u> knows that much, for a lot of possible reasons you might want to play out, and you don't need all those characters fleshed-out at the start of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T04:45:32-07:00","id":996024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=996018#post996018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But how many of them actually know even an approximation of those numbers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots? I remember it being pretty common knowledge when I was at school.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's hardly the biggest issue in the world. It's just for that moment when a player asks a NPC how many people are in the consilium. Saying &quot;well, they tell you a number, but I'm not going to tell you&quot; is not exactly great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T05:19:09-07:00","id":996032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=996024#post996024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's hardly the biggest issue in the world. It's just for that moment when a player asks a NPC how many people are in the consilium. Saying &quot;well, they tell you a number, but I'm not going to tell you&quot; is not exactly great.</div> </div> </div> </div>The storyteller doesn't have to be a jerk about it to leave it open. 'A good amount.' 'Dozens.' 'More than average for a city this size.' 'Less than average, other consilia have made comments.'<br /> <br /> If the player presses, one can simply explain, 'I'm leaving it open in case the game runs long and I want to introduce new characters.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-31-2016, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T05:38:10-07:00","id":996035,"title":"","content":"Those all sound pretty evasive. Your player is going to ask how many 'a good amount' is.<br /> <br /> In anycase, my issue is precisely with that admission that a large part of the setting isn't really established yet. I mean, yeah that's generally how RPGs function, but I'm not all that keen on directly admitting it during the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:05:10-07:00","id":996043,"title":"","content":"It's not that big a deal. Honestly, if you don't know it's okay to tell your players that. I've done it more than once, and have never had a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:16:42-07:00","id":996196,"title":"","content":"I think that deciding estimated numbers - like 'only 10', 'about 50', 'more than 80'. 'something past 100' - is enough malleable, and still not sounding evasive to players. You can, always, have 'and new cabal comes to town - and with her, two rival Pylons that hunted her' to change numbers drastically. Still, <i>some</i> numbers pointing makes community sounds as community, not bunch of random NPCs that are shown only in plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:33:14-07:00","id":996266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=996024#post996024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lots? I remember it being pretty common knowledge when I was at school.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's hardly the biggest issue in the world. It's just for that moment when a player asks a NPC how many people are in the consilium. Saying &quot;well, they tell you a number, but I'm not going to tell you&quot; is not exactly great.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHolds up both hands; &quot;No more than two&quot;.<br /> \u200bMy advice if it really is an issue is to give your consillium an exact and likely small number, than place a neighboring consillium or two that can bleed over into play if more numbers are needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:54:54-07:00","id":996281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=996043#post996043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that big a deal. Honestly, if you don't know it's okay to tell your players that. I've done it more than once, and have never had a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=996196#post996196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that deciding estimated numbers - like 'only 10', 'about 50', 'more than 80'. 'something past 100' - is enough malleable, and still not sounding evasive to players. You can, always, have 'and new cabal comes to town - and with her, two rival Pylons that hunted her' to change numbers drastically. Still, <i>some</i> numbers pointing makes community sounds as community, not bunch of random NPCs that are shown only in plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second both of these. If you genuinely do not have a precise idea, just tell your players. Openness and honesty are really good and, if they still want something, estimates are a good response. Generally speaking, it's not hard to give the right feeling with an estimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T16:50:39-07:00","id":996323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=996043#post996043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that big a deal. Honestly, if you don't know it's okay to tell your players that. I've done it more than once, and have never had a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was a big deal. I just wouldn't consider that solution optimal.<br /> <br /> Actually come to think of it, you can just lie. I mean, if your consilium has 76 members, there's no way your players are going to catalogue and interact with all 76 of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:29:46-07:00","id":996346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place?p=996035#post996035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those all sound pretty evasive. Your player is going to ask how many 'a good amount' is.<br /> <br /> In anycase, my issue is precisely with that admission that a large part of the setting isn't really established yet. I mean, yeah that's generally how RPGs function, but I'm not all that keen on directly admitting it during the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never, ever had a player so decided on knowing the precise number of members of the Concilia, unless she had a pretty good reason to want that information. And to be honest, I think that never a player of mine even made similar question to begging with. You have very strange players...<br /> <br /> So, if you ever need a number to give your players, and you feel they won't accept an evasive answer, just estimate a number and go ahead with it. They won't ever know it unless it becomes a thing in the chronicle, and then the very imprecision of the guess can be a plot element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}